# tests.list -- the test applications `./x test qemu` boots under QEMU after the
# smoke test. Read by tests/qemu/run_tests.sh. Edit by hand. One row per test,
# TAB-separated, six fields:
#
#   name     the <name> in the "TEST <name>: PASS" line. A name ending in _e51 or
#            _u54 names the image <dir>/bin-<e51|u54>/<rest>.elf, any other name
#            <dir>/bin/<name>.elf
#   dir      the example directory, relative to the repository root
#   serial   0..4: which QEMU serial port (MMUART0 .. MMUART4) the verdict is on.
#            A `pass` test must also leave every OTHER port silent.
#            The console of the runtime (System.Text_IO) is the MMUART of the image's hart (hart 1 of
#            a U54 image: serial 1, hart 3: serial 3); most tests report through Bare_Console, which
#            is MMUART0 on every hart, so their serial is 0.
#   expect   pass | xfail | console
#   observe  xfail: a grep -E regexp that MUST match QEMU's
#            `-d int,guest_errors` trace or a serial port -- the signature of the
#            documented failure. console: a grep -E regexp that MUST match the
#            serial port of the row. "-" for a pass row.
#   why      xfail: the documented defect, one line. console: what the line
#            proves. "-" for a pass row.
#
#   A `console` row is a program that ends in the last chance handler of the runtime and so cannot
#   report with Test_Report (see tests/qemu/run_tests.sh): it passes if the line is on its port (the
#   console of the runtime is the MMUART of the hart: 0 on the E51, 1 on U54 hart 1) and the other
#   ports are silent, and fails on a hang, a crash or another message.
#
# The committed list has no `xfail` row: a test that cannot pass is not listed, and the reason is written
# down where the tests are documented, not in a row that hides it (tests/host/qemu_tests fails on an `xfail`
# row of this file). The mechanism stays for the runner's own tests and for a future known defect.
#
# `xfail` is not a skip. The test is still booted, and the run fails if it passes
# (the defect is fixed -- flip the row) or fails in any way other than `observe`
# describes (a different failure is a regression, not a known defect). See the
# comment at the top of run_tests.sh.
#
# The images are built by `./x test qemu` for the harts named in BUILD_HARTS of the
# example's example.conf.
name	dir	serial	expect	observe	why
report_test_e51	examples/report_test	0	pass	-	-
report_test_u54	examples/report_test	0	pass	-	-
